add(251,'screw-coupling','Screw versus cylindrical freedom','Why must the screw joint’s displayed1DOF not be interpreted as two independent freedoms merely because a screw rotates and translates?', ['Its ideal rotation and translation are coupled, unlike the independent P+R cylindrical motions','Any screw joint has no translation','The cylindrical joint also has only1DOF','The screw diagram represents three independent rotations'],0,'One independent coordinate can determine coupled rotation and translation; the source contrasts screw1DOF with cylindrical2DOF.', ['This reconciles the single-DOF screw label with helical motion.','A screw mechanism has coupled axial movement, not no translation.','The source explicitly labels cylindrical P+R as2DOF.','Three rotational freedoms correspond to the spherical example.'],typ='conceptual',assumptions=['Ideal screw with fixed lead; its axial displacement is determined by rotation.','The slide’s Screw(R,1DOF) notation is shorthand, not a complete motion description.'])
