add(259,'planar-3r-transform','Pose of planar frame3','Which pair describes the displayed transform’s position and orientation?', ['Position uses θ1 and θ1+θ2; orientation uses θ1+θ2+θ3','Position and orientation depend on θ3 alone','Position uses θ1+θ2+θ3 in both link terms; orientation uses θ1 alone','Position is (L1+L2,0) for every configuration; orientation is always zero'],0,'The translation column has the first two joint-angle combinations, while the rotation block contains the sum of all three angles.', ['This matches the expanded product.','This omits the preceding joints.','This adds θ3 to translations where the frame3-origin formula does not contain it.','Those values hold only at a particular zero-angle configuration, not generally.'],typ='table',formulas=[planar])
add(259,'frame-origin-tool-offset','Frame origin versus tool point','In the shown model, changing only θ3 while holding θ1 and θ2 fixed has which effect?', ['It changes frame3 orientation but not the position of frame3 origin','It rotates the frame3 origin around joint1 by θ3','It changes L1 and L2 while leaving orientation fixed','It must leave every point attached to link3 fixed'],0,'The displayed position has no θ3, but the rotation depends on θ1+θ2+θ3; a separate tool point with a nonzero offset can still move.', ['This distinguishes an origin from an offset point.','The position formula has no θ3 dependence for this origin.','Revolute motion changes orientation, not the fixed link lengths.','An offset point generally moves as frame3 rotates.'],typ='conceptual',formulas=[planar],assumptions=['Discuss frame3 origin, not an unstated tool tip displaced from that origin.'])
add(259,'planar-3r-transform','Computing a planar-arm pose','For L1=2 m, L2=1 m, θ1=90°, θ2=−90°, θ3=30°, what are frame3 position and orientation?', ['(1,2,0) m and30°','(0,3,0) m and30°','(1,2,0) m and0°','(2,1,0) m and90°'],0,'The first link points along+y and the second along+x; the total angle is30°.', ['Both translation and angle are correct.','This fails to include θ2 in the second-link direction.','This omits θ3 from orientation.','This interchanges the x/y contributions and uses only θ1.'],typ='numerical',steps=['θ1+θ2=0°.','x=2cos90°+1cos0°=1 m.','y=2sin90°+1sin0°=2 m.','Orientation=90°−90°+30°=30°.'],formulas=[planar])
add(259,'frame-origin-tool-offset','Adding a stated tool offset','The planar frame3 origin is (3,0) m and its orientation is90°; a tool lies1 m along its local+x3 axis; where is the tool?', ['(3,1) m','(4,0) m','(3,−1) m','(1,3) m'],0,'Rotate the local offset by90° to obtain (0,1) m, then add the frame3 origin.', ['This rotates and translates the offset correctly.','This adds the local offset as if it were already a base-frame x vector.','This uses a−90° rotation.','This rotates the origin instead of only the local offset and then adding it.'],typ='numerical',steps=['The local offset is (1,0).','Rz(90°)(1,0)=(0,1).','Add (3,0)+(0,1)=(3,1) m.'],formulas=[F('p_tool=p3+Rz(ψ)t3',{'p_tool':'tool position in the base frame','p3':'frame3 origin in the base frame','ψ':'frame3 orientation','t3':'tool offset expressed in frame3','Rz':'planar rotation about z'},{'positions':'m','ψ':'degrees in this example'})],assumptions=['The tool offset is newly specified in this question; it is not included in the slide’s frame3-origin formula.'])
add(260,'rpr-table','RPR joint variables','Which set gives the three independent joint variables of the shown RPR manipulator?', ['θ1, d2, θ3','d1, θ2, d3','θ1, θ2, θ3','a0, α1, L2'],0,'The first and third joints rotate; the middle joint translates.', ['This matches revolute-prismatic-revolute order.','This instead describes prismatic-revolute-prismatic variables.','This would treat the middle prismatic joint as revolute.','Those are fixed geometry parameters in the displayed table.'],typ='table',evidence={260:'RPR DH table: joint1 [α0=0,a0=0,d1=0,θ1]; joint2 [α1=90°,a1=0,d2,θ2=0]; joint3 [α2=0,a2=0,d3=L2,θ3].'})
add(260,'rpr-table','RPR twist and fixed offset','Which constants appear in the displayed RPR table?', ['α1=90°, θ2=0, d3=L2','α1=0, θ2=90°, d3=0','α1=90°, θ2=θ3, d3=d2','α1=θ1, θ2=0, d3=0'],0,'The second row carries a90° twist and zero angle; the third row has fixed offset L2.', ['All three are the stated constants.','This moves the90° twist into a joint-angle entry and drops the fixed offset.','This replaces constants with other variable entries.','The first joint angle is not the fixed link twist.'],typ='table',evidence={260:'Rows [i,α_(i−1),a_(i−1),d_i,θ_i]: [1,0,0,0,θ1];[2,90°,0,d2,0];[3,0,0,L2,θ3].'})
rpr=F('p3=((L2+d2)sinθ1,−(L2+d2)cosθ1,0)',{'p3':'frame3 origin expressed in frame0','L2':'fixed offset d3','d2':'middle prismatic joint displacement','θ1':'first revolute joint angle'},{'p3,L2,d2':'same length unit','θ1':'radians unless marked degrees'},['Use the displayed RPR table and factor matrices.'])
add(261,'rpr-transform','RPR translation from the factor matrices','Which position column follows from the printed RPR factors?', ['((L2+d2)sinθ1,−(L2+d2)cosθ1,0)','((L2+d2)cosθ1,(L2+d2)sinθ1,0)','(L2sinθ3,−L2cosθ3,d2)','(d2sinθ1,−d2cosθ1,L2)'],0,'The90° x twist maps both z offsets into the local−y direction, then the first z rotation yields the stated column.', ['This agrees with the factored product.','This misses the−y direction introduced by the90° twist.','This incorrectly makes frame3-origin position depend on θ3 and places d2 on base z.','L2 lies along the same transformed offset direction, not base z.'],typ='derivation',steps=['Combine the two collinear offsets as s=L2+d2.','After Rx(90°), their vector is (0,−s,0).','Apply Rz(θ1) to obtain (s sinθ1,−s cosθ1,0).'],formulas=[rpr])
add(261,'rpr-source-error','Checking an RPR rotation entry','The expanded RPR matrix prints −cosθ3 in row2,column3; multiplying its displayed factors requires which expression?', ['−cosθ1','−cosθ3','sinθ1 sinθ3','cosθ1 cosθ3'],0,'Column3 of Rx(90°)Rz(θ3) is (0,−1,0); left multiplication by Rz(θ1) makes it (sinθ1,−cosθ1,0).', ['This is the factor-derived entry.','This repeats the inconsistent expanded entry.','This belongs to a different product entry and does not describe column3.','This includes θ3 although the last z rotation leaves column3 unchanged.'],typ='derivation',steps=['Use R=Rz(θ1)Rx(90°)Rz(θ3).','Rz(θ3) leaves the z basis vector unchanged.','Rx(90°)(0,0,1)=(0,−1,0).','Rz(θ1)(0,−1,0)=(sinθ1,−cosθ1,0).'],formulas=[F('R=Rz(θ1) Rx(90°) Rz(θ3)',{'R':'RPR orientation matrix','Rz,Rx':'right-handed elementary rotations','θ1,θ3':'first and third revolute joint angles'},{'angles':'degrees in the90° twist; otherwise radians unless specified'})],assumptions=['Derive from the consistent factor matrices; the expanded row2,column3 has a source typo.'],evidence={261:'Factor product displays Rz(θ1), a second transform with Rx(90°) and translation(0,−d2,0), then Rz(θ3) with z offsetL2. Expanded row2,column3 prints−cθ3, whereas multiplying the factors gives−cθ1.'})
add(261,'rpr-source-error','A rotation-matrix sanity check','Set θ1=0° and θ3=90° in the source’s erroneous third column (sinθ1,−cosθ3,0); why can it not be a valid rotation column?', ['It becomes the zero vector rather than a unit vector','It becomes a unit vector with determinant1','A rotation column is allowed to vanish when two joints are perpendicular','The column must equal the translation vector'],0,'A proper rotation matrix has unit columns; the printed expression becomes (0,0,0), exposing the error.', ['The zero norm directly violates orthonormality.','Its norm is0, not1; determinant1 is therefore impossible.','Joint angles do not permit a zero rotation column.','Rotation directions and translation are separate parts of a homogeneous transform.'],typ='numerical',steps=['sin0°=0 and cos90°=0.','The column is (0,0,0).','Its Euclidean norm is0, but a rotation column must have norm1.'],formulas=[F('||r_j||=1',{'r_j':'any column of a proper rotation matrix','||·||':'Euclidean vector norm'},{'norm':'dimensionless'},['The coordinate frames are orthonormal.'])])
add(261,'rpr-transform','Numerical RPR origin position','For θ1=90°, d2=0.4 m and L2=0.6 m, where is the displayed RPR frame3 origin?', ['(1,0,0) m','(0,1,0) m','(0,−1,0) m','(0.4,0,0.6) m'],0,'The combined offset is1 m; sin90°=1 and cos90°=0.', ['This substitutes into the factor-derived position.','This uses a different orientation convention for the offset.','This retains the−y direction without applying the first90° rotation.','Both offsets lie on the transformed common direction, not separate base axes.'],typ='numerical',steps=['L2+d2=0.6+0.4=1 m.','x=1sin90°=1 m.','y=−1cos90°=0 m; z=0.'],formulas=[rpr])
